\begin{problem}
A standard deck of cards has 52 cards (4 suits of 13 kinds each).
In poker, a full house is 3 of one kind of card and 2 of another kind
(e.g., 5 $\heartsuit$, $5\diamondsuit$, $5 \clubsuit$, $8 \spadesuit$,
$8 \heartsuit$).
How many different full house hands are there?
\end{problem}
\vfill
\vfill

