\begin{problem}
A standard deck of cards has 52 cards (4 suits of 13 kinds each).
In 5-card poker, two pairs is 2 of one kind of card, 2 of another kind, and
1 of a third kind (so that it doesn't become a full house).
(e.g.
$5\heartsuit$,
$5\clubsuit$,
$8\diamondsuit$,
$8\spadesuit$,
$2\spadesuit$)
What is the probability of being dealt 2 pairs?
\end{problem}
\vfill
\vfill



\begin{problem}
Each of these problems deals with probabilities when
four 4-sided dice are rolled.
\begin{enumerate}
\item
What is the probability that the four numbers rolled will all be the same?
% (This is like a mini-Yachtzee.)
\vfill
\item
What is the probability that the four numbers rolled will be distinct?
(no repetitions)
\vfill
\item
What is the probability that at least one 1 and at least one 2 are rolled?
\vfill
\item
Given that at least one 1 and at least one 2 are rolled, what is the probability that
all four numbers will be distinct?
\vfill
\end{enumerate}
\end{problem}



